  "verified": false,
  "notes": "Mapped live against game_plugin.dll 27.0.1+2494687 (the offsets come from RTTI class names and object layouts, not from RVAs, so they should survive small patches). Collections are found by RTTI (layout rttiInstances); no roots needed. Person records (Player, Staff) use their db::PERSON part as the base: +0x288 in db::ACTUAL_PLAYER, +0x100 in db::ACTUAL_NON_PLAYER, +0x380 in db::ACTUAL_PLAYER_AND_NON_PLAYER, +0x440 in db::HUMAN_NON_PLAYER. Player-managers (ACTUAL_PLAYER_AND_NON_PLAYER) are listed as Staff only: their db::PLAYING_DATA sits 0x238 before the person part instead of 0x140, so player-only fields would read wrong for them. Names: the person points at a shared name-table entry whose first qword is the string, so editing a first name renames everyone who shares it. Strings are FM length-prefixed UTF-8 (fmString). Dates count the day of year from 1 (dateDayBase 1); 1/1900 is the empty date. Checked against real birth dates (Haaland, Mbappé, Bellingham, Yamal, Guardiola). CA/PA checked across all 32,631 players (1 <= CA <= PA <= 200). Attributes are bytes in db::PLAYING_DATA (person-0x129 to -0xF4), stored as 1-100 and shown rounded /5. Outfield attributes were matched against four Real Madrid players' screens (Courtois, Huijsen, Mbappé, Espí), each to a single byte. Goalkeeping attributes were matched against Courtois and Lunin, and are the 11 bytes that are high for the 3,341 keepers and near 1 for outfielders. Hidden attributes, positions and feet are not mapped. Feet are bytes -0x111 (left) and -0x110 (right), x5, checked against the five screenshots. Hidden attributes are NOT confirmed by the game (it never shows them); they are inferred from statistics over 32,631 players: Dirtiness (-0x100) tracks Aggression, Versatility (-0xF8) tracks how many positions a player has, Injury Proneness (-0xF9) runs against Natural Fitness. Consistency and Important Matches are -0xFD and -0xFA in some order, so both stay unmapped. Personality is the 8 bytes at person+0x70, unscaled 1-20, read as Adaptability, Ambition, Loyalty, Pressure, Professionalism, Sportsmanship, Temperament, Controversy; this fits the game's personality labels (Courtois 'Profesional' has 18 Professionalism, Mbappé 'Resuelto' 15) but is not proven. Staff CA/PA: i16 at person-0x26/-0x24 (plausible for all 19,681 staff). Staff Adaptability is the same person+0x70 byte as the players' (checked against four Real Madrid staff screens, which also supports the personality order). Other staff attributes sit in db::NON_PLAYING_DATA (person-0xF0 to -0xBD): a 1-20 run that looks uncorrelated and a 1-100 run whose bytes cluster like abilities (e.g. -0xD4/-0xD3 correlate 0.90). The game shows staff attributes only as bands (Élite, Muy bueno, Bueno, Competente, Decente, Del montón) that do not map to fixed values across staff, so they are not labelled yet. Club finances: db::CLUB_FINANCE at club+0x150. The transfer budget appears three times (+0x7C4, +0x7C8, +0x7D4, all £42,951,596 for Real Madrid); the editor writes +0x7C4, still to be checked in game. +0x7CC is the guaranteed minimum for next season, +0x7D0 the % of transfer income given back, +0x814 the weekly wage bill. Balance is the i32 at finance+0xC (£100,461,188 for Real Madrid, matching the game). The wage budget is weekly at +0x808 (£6,284,565 = £27,233,115 a month); +0x834 holds the same figure, apparently next season's budget. The game shows wages per month (weekly × 52 / 12), and its lowercase 'm' means thousands.",
